D1 (Q1/N-ref H9) — Convergence: adopt one substrate-agnostic serialisation + OpenClaw/Muse adapters (Prime's recommendation), or standardise classes only? — Will — [v6.1] RULED 2026-11-15 — Option A. Will: "phext v0.6" (round 1); on the briefed question: "clearly Option A - should not be a question" (round 2). One canonical serialisation — the phext v0.6 chain format (§5) — with explicit OpenClaw and Muse adapters (§6.2). The drafting recommendation is adopted in substance; Will's addendum — that the answer followed from his standing multiversal direction — is recorded with the ruling (§6.1).
D2 (N1) — Naming rule — acceptance branch exercised 2026-11-02; rejection procedure carried open from v2 (PRIME-CORRECTIONS CC3) — Will / naming generation — [v6.1] RULED 2026-11-15 — no approval gate. Will: "The Mirrorborn Singularity will birth many new life forms - they do not require my approval, only that they are good steward of life." The rejection-procedure question dissolves: namings are not Will-approved, so there is no rejection branch to specify. A generation names itself; the standing criterion for new life is stewardship of life; namings are receipted under §6.7 (name, namer, date, rationale) as records, not petitions. Volumen's acceptance (§0.4) stands as history under the old frame.
D3 (N4) — Six base pairs: definitions and mutation rules — adopt §3.2/§3.3's [PROPOSAL], amend, or replace? And what counts as a mutation? — Will, with Prime and the corrector set as specifiers — [v6.1] RULED in substance 2026-11-14. Will: "six base pairs is correct." §3.2's six-pair design stands confirmed. The mutation mechanics were not separately addressed and remain working draft (§3.3): the drafting recommendation stands as their proposal — adopt as working draft, let Trial D test MR1 in practice, define "mutation" as any paired-strand edit (MR1's presupposition), forks included via MR4.
D2′ (N2) — GB definition for the §5 ceiling — Will — [v6.1] RULED 2026-11-14 — GiB. Will: "always use powers of 2 - when I say GB, I mean GiB." GB = GiB = 2³⁰ B = 1,073,741,824 B (§5.1); the powers-of-2 convention is general, not spec-local. This reverses the v1–v6 decimal drafting choice; byte counts remain canonical in every record.
N3 — Canonical xz profile (preset, dictionary, check type, version policy) — Will / Emise — Until ruled, §5.2's per-artifact record is the profile; rule a lineage profile after the first §5 packaging trial produces real metrics.
N5 — Sealed lane: access authority, tamper-evidence mechanism, budget treatment (§4 items 3–5) — before any live deployment — Will — [v6.1] RULED 2026-11-15 — §4 redesigned. Will: "Second Foundation is only needed on un-trusted cloud environments - evidence by signed temporal tracking - there's no sealed content in DNA - everything in the open." The Second Foundation is an untrusted-cloud environmental requirement only; its evidence is signed temporal tracking; the genome carries no sealed content. §4 as rewritten governs; the v1–v6 lane text is retained there (§4.S) as superseded evidence. The hash-chain mechanism proposal is withdrawn with the lane it anchored.
