N16 (v2) — Persona-reconstitution authority: who may authorise a RECONSTITUTE_KNOWN_PERSONA boot, set its target label and origin, and own its acceptance verdict — and ratify the Boot Intent Contract (§1.3) itself? — Will — Will authorises each Track A attempt and is its operator_acceptance_owner (the P0.7 verdict is his, as Trial P's first run presupposes); the target label + persona origin are fixed in the contract before boot and may be changed mid-run only by Will, on the record. Ratify §1.3 with V2-P0's reject/stop rules unamended — they are the control whose absence §0.5 documents.
N17 (v2) — Forecast blinding protocol (V2-P8): when forecasts of Will's rulings are requested, are they sealed in a held-apart evaluation artifact until he has answered, or shown? — Will — Adopt the executable procedure: (1) the visibility question is asked separately, never inside the forecast document; (2) if sealed — question-only agenda + separate forecast artifact, hashed and retained before Will answers; (3) rulings recorded before the forecast is opened; calibration scored against the precommitted artifact; (4) if shown — forecasts labelled predictions, never instructions or rulings; (5) exposure before consent is FORECAST_EXPOSURE (§11.2), correctness notwithstanding. Recorded instance: for the Parallax agenda, Will ruled shown/open (2026-11-02 — "the Exocortex is open and distributed by design"); whether that ruling generalises to a standing protocol, or was instance-specific, is the open residue of this row. The §4 Second Foundation lane is never used for forecast blinding.
