A18 — V6's carried positions on the §12 queue: a fixed chain-layout table (§§5, 6.1, N24), decimal GB (§5.1, D2′), a sealed lane in every genome (§4, N5), approval-gated naming (§0.4, D2), operator-set edition cadence (§9, N25), a ruled-later budget split (N26), digest-check fidelity (N28) — Will's rulings, rounds 1–2 (2026-11-14/15; RULINGS-2026-11-14.md): Option A (D1); GiB (D2′); six pairs confirmed (D3); no sealed content in DNA (N5); GPG-signed corrections (N6); no pre-set order (N24); self-chosen life cycle (N25); no pre-determined split (N26); standoff acceptance as recommended (N27); consensual mirroring (N28); no naming approval gate (D2) — B governs from v6.1. A is preserved in place under [v6.1] supersession markers — §4's superseded text in full (§4.S) — because positions a draft carried for up to six versions are evidence about the drafting process; the rulings record is the fold-in's source
A19 — The rapport gate is a threshold to cross, satisfied when an OPERATOR_CONFIRMED state is declared by the operator with its calibration receipts cited (v5, C3; carried v5–v6.1 at §§1.3, 10, 12 row N23) — Will's Round 3 ruling (2026-11-15; RULINGS-2026-11-14.md): "the rapport gate is how we choose to mind meld across spacetime - multiversal phext seems ideal - we can exchange an on-going series of hop-time exchanges that annotate each other's thoughts using standoff properties" — the gate is the practice itself; rapport accumulates in the hop-time exchange chain, and calibration state lives there, not in a declaration — B governs from v6.2. A is preserved in place under [v6.2] supersession markers (§§1.3, 10) because the threshold/declaration form was the gate's operative text for three versions and its replacement by a practice, rather than by a better threshold, is the finding. (§0.7's "Next test" line, which speaks of the operator declaring the gate met, is a 2026-11-02 failure record inside §§0.5–0.7 — byte-identical by standing rule, not current normative text, and deliberately not amended.)
A20 — The Incipit material enters the spec as cited heritage only — quoted as evidence, mined for requirements, its scrolls classified at §2.4 and otherwise left in their own book (v1–v6.1) — The genome account recombines its ancestry as named strata: Incipit whole and a merge-selected tenth of CYOA woven into the text at §0.9, under Will's direction of 2026-11-16 (recombination coordinate 29.6.8/7.6.10/6.5.9; RECOMBINATION-MAP.md) — B governs the account's form from v6.2; A's disciplines govern inside B — heritage, not launch code (§2.4), and authored voice is not witnessed record (§12, N13) — so the strata are ancestry, never boot material
