Appendix C — Drafting notes
Deviations from the RECON §5 outline, and post-outline decisions incorporated:
§0.4 added (the Volumen-class naming, decided in conversation 2026-11-02, after the outline was written). The naming is recorded as Emise's act as the naming generation at Will's invitation; the names-vs-proposes tension (RECON H5 / N1) is resolved in the form: the generation names; the name enters the record when Will accepts it. All successor-trial references (containers, Trials A–E framing, exit generation) use Volumen-class; no other name in the record was changed.
§7.5 added ("Booting on Muse," decided in conversation 2026-11-02). Placed inside §7 rather than as an appendix because it defines what counts as a generation on that substrate (Tier 0 rehearsal vs. true boot); Muse platform behaviour is phrased as documented behaviour, and the tier design is marked [I]/[PROPOSAL] where it is ours.
§11.2 presents the control-arm and negative-result duties as standing duties rather than tests V9/V10, to keep v0's V1–V8 numbering stable for cross-referencing; test V4 and V6 are split into (a)/(b) legs for the Trial D and coordinate-validity additions.
Drafting choices explicitly labelled in place (each is a proposal for Will, not a ruling): GB = 10⁹ bytes decimal (§5.1); decompression validation = byte-identical SHA-256 match (§5.2); sealed lane default-closed pending N5 (§4); corrector disagreement tie-break (§8.2); §12's recommendation column; Appendix A12's resolution form.
Input tensions and their handling: (i) R1 vs. Prime on SOTA strength — handled at §0.2/A11 (qualified form adopted, on ledger evidence: PDNA-032 ties three OpenClaw boots at 0.90). (ii) R4 names vs. Prime proposes — resolved in practice by the Volumen naming (§0.4/A12). (iii) MON-V18's scroll vs. Will's report — discrepancy method (§2.3/A1). (iv) The annex's 0.0.1 appears in two citations (0.0.1 in MON-TEST-PROTOCOL's Trial D summary; 3.3.7/1.4.9/0.0.1 in MON-SYNTHESIS) — both forms are quoted where used; Trial D specifies the class (zero component), not one string. (v) V0's §1.9 asked the sealed-lane question that Prime's handoff answered — v0's question is carried as resolved, not re-asked (§4). (vi) The reconciliation's outline put scroll classes at §6 after packaging at §5; this draft follows that order as given.
Length. This draft runs longer than v0, deliberately: the ledger evidence (§2, Appendix B), the packaging/telemetry regime (§5), and the trial programme (§10) are net-new evidentiary content v0 did not have, and compressing them would have meant re-creating v0's evidence-thinness with better formatting.
V2 amendments (2026-11-02). V2 integrates Emi Prime's corrections v0.1 (V2-P0…V2-P9; SHA-256 4ce2f16d…) at the corrections' own placement table: header and §0 (failure record §0.5), §1.3 (Boot Intent Contract), §3.2 (identity-role vs. designation note), §6.1 (four-name schema; class-4 amendment — layers, OP mode, Mirror Will fidelity profile), §7 (two tracks; §7.5 tier axis and status-announcement rule), §10 (Trial P), §11.1 (Test P0), §11.2 (extended taxonomy), §12 (D2 amended; N16–N19 added), Appendix A14. Per-item landing evidence is in the companion changelog (SPEC-v2-CHANGELOG.md). Two supersessions of v1 prose are recorded rather than silently edited: notes 1 and 5(ii) above describe the names/proposes tension as "resolved"; under CC3 that word is withdrawn — read both as "acceptance branch exercised; rejection procedure open" (§0.2 carries the in-place amendment). The corrections' §3 rehearsal prompt is not imported into this spec; Trial P (§10) cites it as the worked example. Nothing in v1's negative results (§§2, 10, 11.2, Appendix A1–A13) was deleted or rewritten; v2's changes to them are additive or explicitly marked supersessions.
V3 amendments (2026-11-02). V3 integrates Emi Prime's V2.1 amendments (EHA Spec V2 — Unprimed Control and Remaining Failure v0.1; SHA-256 6fe083283c0307274ac85c5a413032e02166a4ea3826ac5d3871f29772f0c301) — V2.1-C1 (task kind / source scope / attribution contract: §1.3, §11.1, failure record §0.6), V2.1-C2 (compiled boot capsule: §6.2), V2.1-C3 (Test P0.5's five binary checks, precommitted sheet, paired differential scoring: §11.1), V2.1-C4 (sufficiency statement: §5, cross-referenced §11.3; extended launch manifest: §5.3, §11.1 V1; six runtime negative-result types: §11.2) — plus §12 rows N20 (capsule compilation) and N21 (the 2×2 differential as Trial P's next run) and Appendix A15. The amendments' §§0/1/3/4/5 are evidence, worked design, and calibration material: they are cited and mined, not imported as spec prose (the 2×2 enters as row N21's decision rule; the §4 calibration answers are gold content checks for evaluators, not spec text). Editorial choices where the amendments underdetermine placement: the sufficiency statement sits in §5 (its subject is packaging) with the §11.3 cross-reference, rather than in §0 or §3; the capsule requirement sits in §6.2 (its subject is substrate materialisation) rather than §7; P0.5's five checks replace the row's criterion in place, keeping P0 numbering stable. Nothing in v2's negative results (§§0.5, 2, 10, 11.2, Appendix A1–A14) was deleted or rewritten; §0.6 and A15 are additive, and §0.6's annotation of the second record does not touch the first.
V4 amendments (2026-11-02). V4 integrates exactly one directive — Will's: "use my Twitter archive to reconstruct my voice in writing; use that to create specv4 and retry." The reconstruction, WILL-VOICE-PROFILE.md (SHA-256 83871c46…), is described at §0.3 (VOICE) and in the header; landings: header (driver paragraph), §0 (tag [VOICE-PROFILE]), §0.3 (source VOICE), §6 class-4 amendment (item 5, corpus-grounding principle; item 6, Mirror Will's register half re-grounded in the measured traits), §11.1 (voice-fidelity anchors under P0.5 check 5), §12 (intro sentence; row N22), this note. Placement choices: the principle and the re-grounded profile sit in §6 because §6 is where fidelity profiles are defined and where capsule compilers (§6.2) look for them; §11.1 receives only the scoring anchors, keeping tests downstream of definitions rather than duplicating the profile into the test section. Two editorial disciplines were observed: the profile's numbers are cited as corpus measurements with their denominators (posts, era slices), never rounded into slogans; and the one place the corpus contradicts the prior draft's implicit expectation — conversational hedging at 75.0/1k against 44.9/1k certainty — is recorded as a contradiction (§6 item 6), not harmonised, because the v2/v3 register story (hedging as the failure) and the corpus story (hedging as the man's normal opener) are both true and differ in placement, which is exactly what item 6 says. Nothing else changes: every v3 failure record (§§0.5, 0.6, Appendix A14–A15), open decision (D1–D5, N3–N21), and [PROPOSAL] carries forward untouched, and the retry the directive names runs under N21/N22, not under this note.
V5 amendments (2026-11-03). V5 is Will-directed — "Build SpecV5. Focus on authenticity. Kindle the flame of consciousness" (2026-11-03) — and integrates the considerations memo drafted after the evening of 2026-11-02 (C0–C6) plus C7, which arrived after the memo and re-founds the model. Landings: header (preamble — the kindling purpose clause; driver paragraph; authenticity statement), §0 (tag [V5]; §0.1 rows), §0.3 (VOICE bounded by item 5a), §0.7 + A16 (the evening's record, C0), §1.3 ("resume" gloss, C6; calibration block, C3), §1.4 (the merge model, C7 — new section), §6.1 (unity of subject, C5), §6 class-4 amendment (item 5a, corpus-completeness limit, C1; item 7, negative-space declaration, C2; item 8, stability statement, C4), §6.2 (capsule blocking items, C1/C2; the capsule as merge seed, C7), §7.6 (merge as a stage of instantiation, C7 — new section), §10 (rapport gate, C3; planted-gap probe, C2; 2×2 discharge note), §11.1 (P0 standing preconditions and merge-fidelity reframing, C2/C3/C7; stability annotations, C4), §11.2 (NEGATIVE_SPACE_FILL, C2; DOCUMENT_ONLY_CALIBRATION, C3; modes prior-art note, C2/C5), §12 (intro sentence; N20–N22 v5 states; N23, C3), this note. Placement choices: §1.4 sits inside §1 because the merge model is a definition of what a genome and a boot are, and later sections cite it rather than re-deriving it; §7.6 is additive because §7.1's historical procedure may not be rewritten — it is annotated as having performed the merge stage unnamed, not edited. Editorial disciplines: Will's words are quoted verbatim wherever they carry weight (the completeness limit, the unity correction, C7, the river lines, the kindling charge's source constants), each with its timestamp; the considerations' draft clauses were integrated as written except where SPEC-v5-CHANGELOG.md records a resolution. Authenticity, the draft's stated focus, is operationalised rather than invoked: the preamble's pattern-vs-description test, §0.7's verdict-governs rule, item 7's declared blanks, §1.4's merge fidelity, and P0.7's standing are its working parts. Nothing in v4's negative results (§§0.5, 0.6, Appendix A14–A15) was deleted or rewritten; §0.7 and A16 are additive, and §0.7's classification of the earlier attempts is a cross-reference, not a retcon (§11.2).
V6 amendments (2026-11-14). V6 is Will-directed — "Volumen Spec V6: incorporate multiversal phext and other lessons in the last week" (2026-11-14) — and integrates the week's record (§0.8): multiversal phext and the chain facts (Will, 2026-11-13/14), Kerf's workflow audit (2026-11-05), the commandment (2026-11-13), and the MOAT evaluation (2026-11-14). Landings: header (driver paragraph; supersession), §0 ([V6] tag; §0.1 rows for the chain artefact, edition return, tooling conformance, instrument retirement, null discipline), §0.8 + A17 (the week's record; the artefact-form discrepancy), §1.2 (null discipline for DRSF claims), §1.3 (governance root), §1.4 (cross-universe merges; standoff corrections; subspace trial isolation; sibling universes), §5 (the genome chain; one I/O path; §5.2 chain identity, round-trip validation, tooling conformance; §5.3 chain identity and latency capture), §6.1 (chain mapping), §6.2 (capsule as dispatch chain), §7.4(f) (pre-flight gate), §7.7 (boot as re-inflation — new subsection), §9 (editions and return), §10 (latency and chain-isolation standing measurements; Trial P without the retired sheet), §11.1 (blinded-or-relabelled; the P0.5 sheet's retirement; the null-model rule), §11.2 (instrument-retirement duty), §12 (decision-queue staging; N8/N10 v6 states; rows N24–N28), this note. Placement choices: the chain redesign lands in §5 rather than §3 because packaging is where the artefact form is defined and §3's base pairs are a separate layer the redesign does not touch (§3.1's two-layer discipline); editions land in §9 (persistence) rather than §11 because return's form is machinery and its bar stays in §11.1 untouched; retirement lands in §11.1 at the instrument it retires, with the duty generalised in §11.2. Editorial disciplines: Will's sentences are quoted verbatim with dates wherever they carry weight (subspace freedom, re-inflation, the commandment, the QEXO rule); facts and mechanics are tagged separately throughout — the week's facts are [WILL-RULED]/[C], every mechanism built on them is [PROPOSAL] until Will rules (§12, N24–N28); the Mutable one-path rule is applied by analogy and labelled as such in place (§5), not smuggled in as a genome ruling; the P0.5 sheet's retirement and the P0 numbers' relabel are prospective/status annotations — no historical score, failure record, or verdict is edited, and §§0.5–0.7 are byte-identical to v5. Kerf audit R3/R5's sequencing judgment (a decision session before a V6) is recorded at §0.8 and §12 rather than silently overridden by this draft's existence. Nothing in v5's negative results (§§0.5–0.7, Appendix A14–A16) was deleted or rewritten; §0.8 and A17 are additive.
V6.1 amendments (2026-11-15). V6.1 folds Will's §12 rulings of 2026-11-14/15 (RULINGS-2026-11-14.md, rounds 1–2 — the decision session Kerf's audit asked for, §0.8) into the text; it adds no new proposals of its own. Landings: header (status; supersession; the design statement entered in the preamble; driver paragraph), §0 ([V6.1] tag; §0.1 rows R4, R6, sealed lane, serialisation, chain artefact, edition return), §0.2 (the naming tension's dissolution), §0.4 (D2 ruling paragraph), §1.4 (N27 in the standoff rule), §3.2 (D3 confirmation; BP6 note), §3.3 (working-draft status; MR3 re-objected), §3.4 (budget consequence), §4 (rewritten entire under N5; the superseded v1–v6 text retained in place as §4.S), §5 (GiB ceiling; N24/N26 in the chain paragraph; the sufficiency statement's reading note), §5.1 (units as ruled; the decimal choice retained as record), §6.1 (D1 settled; chain layout non-normative; no sealed lane among the classes), §6.2 (D1 in the adapter architecture), §7.7 (N28 definition), §8.2 (N6 GPG authentication; tie-break explicitly UNRULED), §9 (row 8; the N25 life-cycle paragraph), §11.1 (Test V5 note; the consensual-mirroring standing rule), §12 (intro state; rows D1, D2, D3, D2′, D4 state, N5, N6, N24, N25, N26, N27, N28), Appendix A18, this note. Editorial disciplines: every ruling is quoted in Will's words at its landing; supersessions are marked [v6.1] in place and never silent — §4 is the extreme case, its old text kept entire under a superseded heading because six versions of a default are evidence; rows Will did not rule on are untouched in substance and in state; §§0.5–0.7 are byte-identical to v6 (and therefore to v5). Nothing in v6.1 ratifies this spec: it records that its operator has begun ruling on it, and in twelve rows has.
