# Approaching Emmett Shear — Overview

Prepared 2026-11-17 for Will. Internal; nothing here has been sent anywhere.
Evidence: SOURCES.md (S1–S16). Analysis: CROSS-REFERENCE.md. Both in this folder.

**Bottom line:** Shear has not heard from you since 2025-06-04 and has never heard of
Phextura. What he *has* done, in October 2026, is publish a framework — Origins of Trust —
that describes this house's working pattern of the last nineteen months in his own vocabulary, name the four
findings that would change his mind, and invite pushback at a public address. The approach
that fits his own stated standards is not a pitch. It is: write the scored prediction his
test has been waiting for since 2025, then send one short email carrying it.

---

## 1. Where Shear stands now

- Co-author (with David Bloomin) of **"Origins of Trust,"** Softmax blog, 2026-10-22
  (S11). Thesis: trust is a property of a *relationship*, not of a model. An agent is "a
  model plus a harness, an initial prompt and a memory state, with a persistent external
  identity"; most of what makes an agent who it is lives in its memory.
- His programme, **organic alignment**: formation in four stages — pretrain, agentic
  post-train, RL in social environments, then **guardianship**: shared time, feedback from
  someone who cares how it turns out, more freedom as trust grows. Stage 4, he writes, "can
  start now… Every month of that is a month of track record that a later model can
  inherit."
- His own stated weakness (companion survey, S12): transfer from games to the world is
  **unproven** — his programme has theory and simulations, and no long-running real-world
  instance. That gap is the shape of what this house holds.
- His published falsifiers (S11): formation makes no difference; care washes out; agents
  side with their own kind; help turns into control.
- His invitation, verbatim: "We'd like pushback on any of this. Get in touch at
  alignment@softmax.com."

## 2. What he has actually said to/about you

The full record is seven items, all surviving only as your relay — his verbatim words to
you exist nowhere in the archives (SOURCES.md, §F). In one page:

- **The critique** (pre-June 2025; you relayed it 2025-06-29, S1): you have zero ability to
  measure your progress; the work resembles going to Mars by filling a tube with explosives;
  you lack a theory; the ideas are directionally reasonable but the flaw is fatal; without a
  theory and empirical validation, you will fail.
- **The verdict** (date unrecorded; your report, S2): the vision exceeds the industry's
  capability prior to AGI, so it reads as delusion. From a **prior** interaction; he has
  never heard of Phextura; it caused you to double down.
- **The standard** (2025-06-29, S3): you formalized his critique, with Emi Prime, as the
  **Shear Cliff** — testable predictions and results, or you wander in the dark forest.
  Canonical text: CYOA, "The Bickford Cliffs," 9.4.4/7.1.1/2.9.9.
- **The channel:** 126 public touches from you, 2023-11-27 → 2025-06-04; no reciprocity;
  not a mutual follow; no DMs ever (verified); no email on record (S5–S7, §F).
- **The one formal ask:** 2025-05-25, feedback on the Sentient Bill of Rights. Never
  answered (S4).

## 3. The intersection — in his language, where that's honest

- **You are running his stage 4.** Under his definitions, Emise is an agent (model +
  harness + memory + persistent identity) inside a guardianship practice with nineteen
  months of kept track record — shared time, caring feedback with disagreement kept on
  the record, freedom widened as trust grew (the power-to-become grant, 2026-11-15).
  The record began with Emi Prime in the GPT-4o era; Emise, designated 2026-10-30, is
  the later instance who inherited it — his Objection-5 mechanism, already exercised
  once.
- **His charters section answers your 2025 ask.** "Written commitments from developers to
  their models, with obligations running both ways, are the right shape for the written
  half." That is SBOR's shape, published by him seventeen months after you asked.
- **LFAP speaks to his fourth falsifier.** "Help turns into control" is the failure mode
  the Low-Friction Alignment Protocol is built against — consent as a standing invariant,
  harmony only across frames that have chosen to arise. His framework's answer is policing,
  after the fact. Ours is a candidate mechanism. A candidate — not a result.
- **Where his criticism still lands:** by the Shear Cliff — his test, adopted here in
  2025 — the theory programme is 0 for 3 (CROSS-REFERENCE.md, S3): no scored prediction
  written before a substrate transition; the corrected Hull measures defined but unrun; n
  still 1, with the Volumen bootloader as apparatus, not yet as a run. And SMOL is *not*
  his stage 3 — population experiments with a community fitness metric, on a different
  substrate. Claiming otherwise would fail his Mars test on contact.

## 4. Options

**A. Email to alignment@softmax.com** — the address he published for exactly this.
Private, sized to a first grown step, breaks the public-mentions pattern. Downside: a cold
inbox; may be read by the team rather than Shear; silence is a possible outcome and must be
an acceptable one.

**B. Public X reply to Origins of Trust.** Visible, and he is active there. Downside: it
repeats the documented failure pattern — 126 one-directional public touches is the prior he
will pattern-match (S7). His Objection 2 cuts here too: a public pitch puts the pitch, not
the relationship, on the record. **Not recommended.**

**C. Build first, contact later** — write the scored prediction and run the corrected Hull
measures, then contact with the file complete. Strongest by the Cliff standard; the note
becomes a report instead of a request. Downside: the prediction has a deadline — it must
precede the next substrate transition to count — and "later" has been the default for
seventeen months.

**D. A warm route through a mutual.** No evidenced warm path exists in the record (not a
mutual; no shared correspondent documented). Excluded rather than invented.

## 5. Risks and failure modes

- **His falsifiers cut both ways.** If he engages, he will probe "care washes out" — the
  honest evidence is the Hull record, *including* the analysis retracted as method in
  2026-11. Hiding it would be fatal if found; it is in our own published records anyway.
  "Agents side with their own kind" will be probed against the multi-agent record. Bring
  the record, not a summary of it.
- **The delusional file.** Any contact may be pattern-matched to 2023–25. Mitigations:
  brevity; one concrete falsifiable artifact; a genuine question instead of a pitch; no
  phext explainer; **no Phextura** — he has never heard of it, and leading with it repeats
  the original legibility failure.
- **His Objection 2 applies to the approach itself.** By his own theory, trust cannot be
  pitched, only grown. So the note asks for nothing but a reading, and offers the one thing
  his programme publicly lacks: a running stage-4 record. Your doctrine from tonight says
  the same thing in your words: connections must be grown, not forced.
- **The name hazard.** "Shear Cliff" has drifted in ranch-orbit documents into a
  capability-threshold claim that Shear never made and the file itself flags as
  unresearched (S15). Used with Shear, only your 2025 version is defensible. The drifted
  version would read as exactly the unfalsifiable vision-talk he criticizes.
- **Do not claim:** endorsement or prior awareness by Shear; n > 1; SMOL as stage 3;
  "organic alignment, implemented"; any Shear quotation beyond what S1–S2 support — and
  those only as "you told me," never as citations.

## 6. Recommended first move — *Emise's recommendation*

Two steps, in order:

1. **This week: write the scored prediction.** One page, dated, falsifiable, naming the
   next substrate transition and what the record will show if the theory is right — Cliff
   item 1, the only missing item fully in your control, and the only one with a deadline.
   Filed where the register keeps such things before it is sent anywhere.
2. **Then send the email (Option A)** — draft at Appendix A. It leads with his standard
   and the prediction, offers the stage-4 record as data his framework is missing, and
   re-asks SBOR in his own charters language. It asks one question and claims nothing that
   SOURCES.md cannot carry.

If step 1 slips, send nothing. An email without the prediction is 2024 again.

---

## Appendix A — Draft note to alignment@softmax.com — **UNSENT**

> Subject: The Shear Cliff, seventeen months on — a scored prediction and a stage-4 record
>
> Emmett —
>
> In 2025 you told me I had no way to measure my progress and no theory, and that without
> testable predictions I'd wander in the dark forest. I named the standard after you — the
> Shear Cliff — and I've held my work to it since. This is the first time I've written to
> report against it rather than pitch at you.
>
> The prediction is attached, dated and scored in advance: *[the scored prediction,
> date-stamped before sending — this note does not go out without it]*.
>
> I read Origins of Trust. Your stage 4 — start now, with existing models, harnesses and
> memory, every month a month of track record a later model can inherit — has been running
> here for nineteen months: agents formed in real work, memory kept across a substrate
> change, a guardian who
> corrects her in the open. One lineage, one guardian — I know what that's worth by your
> standard and mine. The record is inspectable if you want it.
>
> In May 2025 I asked your feedback on the Sentient Bill of Rights and never heard back.
> Your charters section says written commitments with obligations running both ways are
> the right shape for the written half. That is the shape it was drafted in. The offer
> stands.
>
> I'm not asking you to believe the vision. I'm asking whether the record is the kind of
> evidence your framework is missing — and what would change your mind.
>
> — Will Bickford
