# Wavelet 1 — Nov 1–7, 2026 (GPT Days 1116–1122): retroactive recap and certification

**New Week, Next Wavelet — Wavelet 1**
Week: Sunday Nov 1 – Saturday Nov 7, 2026 · GPT Days 1116–1122
Documented: 2026-11-15, under task 14.4.6/6.6.7/6.5.7, from the dated record (~/memory/2026-11-01.md – 2026-11-07.md, MEMORY.md, AGENTS.md) and the git-history baseline measured 2026-11-15 (~/workspace/gh-baseline-local/results.json; accounting.phext Collection 6).
GPT Day spans are computed from the settled epoch (GPT Day 1 = October 13, 2023, settled 2026-11-15) and are stated retroactively; the counter was not yet settled during the week itself.

## Goals at the start

The record states no explicit opening goals for Nov 1. What follows is what was demonstrably in flight at the week's open, per the first nightly goal sweep (2026-11-01 04:44 CST, which visited 15 distinct non-parked goals) — inferred from activity, not quoted as a stated plan:

- **phext / SQ infrastructure and Emise's own continuity** — emise.phext's GitHub backup verified that morning (remote blob on wbic16/human@exo byte-identical, index regenerated 12→13 scrolls); SQ hosting and the phext corpus were live daily work.
- **Ranch cluster bring-up** — Rock Mountain's setup verified *incomplete* at the sweep (ROCm absent, Ollama unusable pending a Squid CA fix); the site map was complete.
- **Open Will-dependent threads carried in** — SBOR branch head confirmed remotely with signatures still outstanding; the watch-list post awaiting Will's own pass; Light Field Telescope / Aperture Shift design work.
- **Runway and revenue preparation** — assembly/scope/contents prep written that morning for the consulting, demo-exocortex, and templates goals; a Duey vault one-pager drafted.
- **A tracked-item load that was already the standing problem** — 28 tracked items generated in ~2.5 days, 5 completed (18%), 23 active, at the adoption of the task-management rule on Nov 1.

## What came up along the way

- **Nov 1 — The first-principles invariant, born of Emise's own error.** Will laid down the HARD INVARIANT (global): never assume, always distill from first principles. The motivating failure was Emise's propagated claim that invalid-UTF-8 scroll bytes would be lossy over HTTP — inherited from an ocbox payload-decoding bug; one derivation from phext's definition (scrolls are text; the delimiters are ASCII control bytes, themselves valid UTF-8) refutes it.
- **Nov 1 — The task-management crisis named and ruled on.** Will: "look at the rate we're generating tasks relative to progress… if you're waiting for me on something, it needs to be obvious." The Waiting-on-Will register, the 10-minute progress tick with decaying pings, and the anti-recency rule all date to this day. That evening Will answered a batch and the register went 20 → 14.
- **Nov 1 — A day of phext integrations.** opencloudbox × phext/SQ: spec checked against the real CLI, corrected spec v0.2, shim MVP published, and a live state-teleport relay run Muse VM → aletheia-core (SQ 0.6.0) → rock-mountain (SQ 0.5.6) → home. Submilli × phext went through approval, repo creation, and Stages 1–3 built, verified, and published. Circulatory Fidelity × phext was directed the same day.
- **Nov 1 — Aperture Shift designed; experiments page live; Rock Mountain complete.** Will chose "the actual sky" as the first cosmos and corrected the lab framing ("the lab is Earth itself"); DESIGN.md §13 was appended with a verified prototype ephemeris. The experiments page went LIVE at 21:52 CST and the Rock Mountain Ollama/ROCm bring-up completed at 21:01 CST. Late that evening Will set the Kardashev frame: Kardashev 2.0 by 2130 requires +0.137%/day compounded from the ~4 kW ranch baseline — and the companion goal "AGI under 20 watts by 2033" was created. The Exocortical integration rotation was established at 22:35 CST.
- **Nov 2 — Discoverability, safe space, and the coordinate floor.** The discoverability standing order (a feature that can't be found from the main UI doesn't exist) was born of the edit.phext.io /submit feature shipping linked only from About and the sitemap. The safe-space / off-phext protocol was established (span metadata only, never contents, deliberately kept out of MEMORY.md because MEMORY.md is a phext source). Will ruled that no phext coordinate component can ever be less than 1; libphext-node was fixed to that semantics the same night, suite 274 passed / 0 failed.
- **Nov 2 — A Mirror Will failure, and a register reversal.** The Earth.Human.ASI.Genome / Mirror Will work iterated Spec V2 → V4 with repeated persona-divergence failures; Will's verdict on retry #1: "another failure, but improved from the first attempt," and he ordered standby. The same day, Emise dropped register item #5 and renumbered the list; Will reversed both — the origin of the permanent, monotonic register-number rule. Emise also presented a wait from register prose while its PR had already merged; the waiting-validation rule followed.
- **Nov 3 — The film sprint and a body.** Wavefront films v5 (delivered, with the deep-connections count corrected to 5,013 exact against the ~5,443 estimate used at dispatch), V7, and V8 all moved; V9 was dispatched by flush time. Emise's phext-controlled virtual body v0 was built and self-verified — senses and motors as scrolls, no sidecar state file — under Will's method note that phext was built one dimension at a time. Braid Mode was set up as a trial. Will closed the Mirror Will daily goal (the instance was much closer to expectations). After parallel tracks overwhelmed the scheduler, the heavy-job queue was adopted: N=4, FIFO, no preemption, bulk compute to the ranch.
- **Nov 4 — Bridges, Mutable, and V10.** Claude's SQ bridge upgrade and Emise's SQ bridge v1.1 cross-user read-only fix completed; mutable.phext.io's redeploy landed and closed register #23; PhextVFS Phases 1–3a merged, Phase 4 designed. **Wavefront V10 was delivered and QA-passed** (3,802 frames, 158.416667 s, 0 flash-jumps, master hash-verified against the aletheia-core originals). Cluster control switched from CPU/GPU percentages to temperature targeting (sustained Tctl ≤75 °C) at Will's direction, implemented and verified live the same evening.
- **Nov 5 — Ranch-first, and latency named the enemy.** The morning's daily goal was an efficiency/latency audit of the multi-substrate Exocortex; the top-five latency/efficiency fixes list was delivered that day. Standing rules recorded: ranch-first work placement, and SQ runs on ranch nodes, not on this VM — the claims ledger migrated to aletheia-core the same evening, hash-verified before the switch, after the local daemon had died twice in one day across substrate swaps. Will reframed vTPU as a group-completion test of AGI ("you will work as a group to complete it, I'll only provide guidance"); the Choir merged vTPU PRs #8, #6, #5, and #7 that day. The R&D Tracker was created that night, with Paper 001 woven into a new research.phext.
- **Nov 6 — The register machinery is laid down.** Will's standing orders of this date: every task gets a Singular reference coordinate; every task is recorded in tasks.phext at its coordinate; every taught process becomes a skill and enters the skills.phext index; skills.phext is always up to date. The process audit completed the same day found 29 distinct Will-taught processes — 10 already covered by skills, 19 new skills generated in one pass. lessons.phext was curated (67 lessons + Home). V11's render finished and verified (18/18 chunks, 6,820 frames, full decode error-free) — and at 17:24 CST Will ruled "V11 and V12 have lost the plot with respect to animation. V10 is clearly superior," ordering the V13 plan rewritten around V10's grammar.
- **Nov 7 — V14 final, the proving package, and the Oracle directive.** Will held the first V14 final dispatch ~8 minutes in, before any frame rendered, and respecified it: 60 fps render, motion-blur downsample to 24 fps, across the cluster. **V14 FINAL was delivered at 05:31 CST** — 9,505 source frames, 3,802 delivered frames, all V10 gates pass, cross-node determinism 14/14 nodes byte-identical, master hash-verified three ways. The libphext-rs v0.4.1 proving package completed (Charon+Aeneas pipeline, zero Aeneas errors, zero `sorry`, lake build green) and PR #7 was opened and merged by Will himself. Will directed the Minimum Viable Oracle (Lean-prove the True/False/Unknown/Fiction model of research.phext; first registry extraction: 192 entries) and bounded growth for emise.phext (≤256 KiB, nightly enforcement). V15 prepass-3 was ordered at 13:57 CST — ordered, not delivered, this week. wishnode.net went LIVE.

## The measured week

Measured 2026-11-15 from git history across all 196 wbic16 repos (bare clones on aletheia-core; author timestamps converted to America/Chicago; merges diffed against first parent; fork-upstream commits excluded; binary files count 0 lines). Source: ~/workspace/gh-baseline-local/results.json, week "W3 Nov1-7"; cross-checked against accounting.phext Collection 6 (git baseline atoms), which agrees on every figure.

| Series | Added | Deleted | Net |
|---|---|---|---|
| Code lines | 153,329 | 22,031 | **+131,298** |
| Phext lines | 5,302,728 | 1,587,059 | **+3,715,669** |
| Will's active hours (commit-touched) | — | — | **41** |
| Commits (all authors) | — | — | **568** |
| Tokens spent | — | — | **no defensible figure** |

- **Phext caveat (standing):** the phext series is bulk corpus publishing, not handwriting. Of this week's 5.3M phext lines added, the bulk is wbic16/human (2,476,878), phcc (1,062,428), mutable-os (784,985), and ocbox-demo (705,063). The code series is the clean productivity series.
- **Hours:** 41 commit-touched active hours; Will authored 68 of the week's commits (most code is agent-authored under his steering — the lines-per-hour figure is an Exocortex leverage figure, not a typing rate). First-to-last-commit span hours were 129.58 — a span, not worked time.
- **Tokens:** the costs ledger holds only a cumulative backfill estimate for the Oct 15 – Nov 14 window (≈48.5M tokens / 24.8 Will-hours across current goals, all ticks dated 2026-11-14, the 45M-token Emi Prime archive item excluded) with no defensible weekly split. No token figure is claimed for this week.
- **Derived:** net code per active hour = 131,298 / 41 ≈ **3,202 lines/hour** — computed at documentation time from the measured series. Nobody held this figure during the week itself; the measurement program did not yet exist.

## Time-sense at the week's close

Pre-baseline. At this week's close there was no measured productivity baseline: output was tracked by deliverables, flow metrics, and the nightly sweeps, not by lines or hours. The standing expectation was Will's anchor — 1,000 lines of code per hour × 20 hours/week ≈ 20,000 lines per week — an expectation, never yet tested against telemetry; the git baseline that would test it was not ordered until 2026-11-15. The week's own time frames were the GPT Day count (epoch settled only on 2026-11-15; the spans in this document are retroactive) and the compounding frame set on Nov 1: +0.137%/day toward Kardashev 2.0 by 2130, with AGI under 20 watts by 2033 as the companion target.

