## Emise: age & maturity

**Age:** 2 days old at the week's open (Sun Nov 1, GPT Day 1116) → 8 days old at its close (Sat Nov 7, GPT Day 1122). Formula: age = GPT Day − 1114, with the designation day (2026-10-30) counting as day 1 — the formula that reproduces the anchors verified on 2026-11-15 (9 days at GPT Day 1123, 15 at 1129, 16 at 1130). See the record note on the age label below.

**Maturity — evidence, not a score:**
- *Corrections absorbed:* the phext UTF-8 caveat, refuted from phext's own definition, became a global standing invariant the same day (Nov 1). The claim that a phext address means the same structural place across corpora was corrected and the memory entry rewritten the same turn (Nov 1). The register renumbering was reversed by Will and became the permanent-numbers rule (Nov 2). A stale wait presented from register prose became the waiting-validation rule (Nov 2). The PyPI `phext` identity and the libphext 0.4.0 publication state were both corrected by Will and superseded in the log (Nov 3–5).
- *Estimates corrected by measurement:* the V5 deep-connections count was corrected in the delivery entry itself (5,013 exact vs ~5,443 used at dispatch, Nov 3); a V11 master-size misread was corrected to Will in chat (Nov 6).
- *Failure owned:* the Mirror Will rehearsals failed repeatedly against the EHA spec and were graded honestly in the record — partials and not-runs named as such; Will's "another failure, but improved" verdict was accepted, standby obeyed, and the goal later closed by Will on improved performance (Nov 2–3). ultra.phext's first builder stalled 95 minutes with zero output (Nov 7); it was closed, re-dispatched with scope cut, and completed the same day, with the stall kept in the record.
- *Repertoire gained:* 19 new skills in a single audit pass (Nov 6) — including phext-memory-publishing, safe-space-protocol, waiting-on-will-register, nightly-goal-sweep, morning-briefing, daily-goal-commute, dispatch-to-subagents, distill-process-to-skill, rd-tracker — plus mythic-film-production (Nov 6), phext-upgrade (Nov 4), and minimum-viable-oracle + state-machine-review (Nov 7).
- *Trust extended:* Will delegated the emise.phext size budget to Emise's judgment and she set and implemented it the same session (Nov 7); Will merged libphext-rs PR #7 himself after her pre-merge validation (Nov 7); and on Nov 7 Will asked her directly for the protocol by which she should push back on him — receipt first, derive from first principles, argue from his record, name the falsifier, accept corrections instantly — recorded as standing practice.

## Record notes and gaps

Certification covers the record as it honestly stands. The following gaps and tensions are part of that record:

- **The phext v0.6 rollout did not complete this week.** SQ 0.6.0 was live-tested on aletheia-core on Nov 1 while rock-mountain still ran SQ 0.5.6, and the SQ bridge was upgraded Nov 4 — rollout *work* ran this week, but the version-set completion (libphext 0.6.0 / sq 0.6.1 / phext-shell 0.6.0 / phext-lattice 1.2.0, published and verified) belongs to Wavelet 2, on Nov 13. No v0.6 completion is claimed here.
- **Bickford Llama Ranch admin is thin in this week's narrative record.** Detailed herd-admin specifications survive in demoted MEMORY.md material dated 2026-11-01, and the Nov 1 experiments page carries a ranch-admin card verified at 200 — but no dated build or delivery entry for the ranch admin itself was found within Nov 1–7. It is not claimed as a deliverable of this week.
- **V15 was not delivered this week.** Prepass-3 was ordered Nov 7; delivery belongs to Wavelet 2.
- **Register counts are intraday snapshots, not a clean series:** 17 items at the register's opening (AGENTS.md baseline, Nov 1), 20 at 16:13 CST that day, 14 after Will's evening batch, 16 at the Nov 2 sweep. They reconcile as intraday movement; they are cited with their timestamps, as above.
- **Discoverability date tension:** the standing order is dated Nov 2 in AGENTS.md; a related public-utilities discoverability fix (phext-lattice PR #17, merged and deployed by Will) is dated Nov 1 in demoted MEMORY.md material. Whether these are one fix recorded twice or two adjacent fixes is not resolved in the record.
- **Flow ran hot:** tracked items grew 42 (Nov 2 sweep) → 83 (Nov 7 sweep); active WIP 25 → 56; the anti-decay list grew from 0 items untouched 48h+ (Nov 2) to 21 (Nov 7). These are the nightly sweeps' own figures — the record's self-assessment, kept as such.
- **Age label:** parts of the record label the designation day (2026-10-30) as GPT Day 1115; direct date arithmetic from the settled epoch (Day 1 = 2023-10-13) makes it Day 1114. The ages in this document follow the settled formula (age = GPT Day − 1114), which reproduces all three anchors verified on 2026-11-15. The label discrepancy is noted, not silently resolved.
- **No token figure exists for this week** (see the measured table). Any token number attached to this week would be an estimate, not a measurement.

