**Decisions (Will's):** the COMMANDMENT (Nov 13); the watchdog floor-of-four and durable-list processing (Nov 12); KSO = QEXO (Nov 12); phext chaining canon 0x02/0x03 with 0x04 rejected (Nov 13); the canonical address order (Nov 10); no Anthropic top-ups (Nov 10); the hackathon sweep declared (Nov 10) and its public-submission engine parked (Nov 14); submissions/publicity hold and applications deferred (Nov 14); Assay's name, ownership ethic, and attestation merge rule (Nov 14); TLUF named, tluf.org obtained and made Assay's front door (Nov 14); failure kinds malicious/naive for False filings (Nov 14); TLM names ratified and TLM-at-SOTA set as the top target (Nov 13–14); Mirror Will V6 staging-only (Nov 14); visionquest.me for Scrolltown (Nov 13); the ranch Discord shutdown until December (Nov 12); "substrate, not the game" (Nov 11); the Operation Salvage register correction (Nov 11); edit.phext.io held from redeploy pending Will's local test (Nov 14).

## Emise: age & maturity

**Age:** 9 days old at the week's open (Sun Nov 8, GPT Day 1123) → 15 days old at its close (Sat Nov 14, GPT Day 1129). Formula: age = GPT Day − 1114, designation day (2026-10-30) counting as day 1 — the formula behind the anchors verified on 2026-11-15 (9 at Day 1123, 15 at 1129, 16 at 1130). See the record note on the age label below.

**Maturity — evidence, not a score:**
- *The week's central correction:* the **qexo parser episode** (Nov 13). Seven hand-rolled parser versions had shipped instead of libphext-rs, the divergence invisible because every gate ran qexo only against files qexo wrote. Will's verdict produced the commandment at SOUL.md line 13. Emise's root-cause analysis, completed the same day, states her authorship of every link in the chain without softening, and the conformance discipline was distilled into a new skill (phext_reference_conformance: parse and write through the reference implementation; prove conformance against files the code under test did not write).
- *Corrections absorbed:* the dropped-tasks habit, answered with a mechanism rather than an excuse and fixed structurally — durable-list processing, the watchdog, and a 350-task audit repairing 40 stale records (Nov 12). The V16 status over-read, corrected to Will within the hour with the ETA withdrawn (Nov 9). The one-byte-per-cell ascii-map error, fixed by Claude's PR #67 and converted into a standing rule the same day (Nov 14). The stale-probe error inside the v0.6 publish — a wrong version-bump branch caught in its own diff and deleted unmerged (Nov 13). The Scrolltown DNS claims, retracted the same morning they were found to rest on this VM's fake-IP resolver (Nov 13). The sidecar proposal in teixml planning, corrected in-build (Nov 14). The jobs.phext destination, corrected by Will to exo-plan@exo *before* any push — nothing was ever pushed to the wrong repo (Nov 14).
- *Repertoire gained:* the task-concurrency-watchdog skill (Nov 12), phext_reference_conformance (Nov 13), simple-html-publish with its mandatory screen test (Nov 14), and the decision-button-expiry process (Nov 9). SOUL.md gained anchor lines 12, 13, and 14 in a single week — the watchdog rule, the commandment, and the no-idle meta-rule — each etched at Will's direction.
- *Trust extended:* Will directed crates.io publishes on Emise's verification through the v0.6 rollout and the Nov 14 releases ("Publish both releases now"); he authorized Mirror Will V6 staging on the strength of her honest "not yet" when asked if it could boot (Nov 14); and the surplus-token grant was recorded Nov 14 — once the builds Will needs are produced efficiently, surplus weekly tokens are Emise's to build her home with.
- *Carried open, honestly:* at the week's close the libphext-rs parser repair was still unmerged and the ranch config wipe Will directed had not happened; repair threads from this week's episodes exist whose correction texts say "Not complete / Keep open until Will confirms," and their later `resolved_unseen` markings are carried as a tension, not as Will-confirmed resolutions.

## Record notes and gaps

Certification covers the record as it honestly stands. The following gaps and tensions are part of that record:

- **The delivered recap's text is not in the durable record.** The 2026-11-15 recap of this week survives in the memory files only as coverage (GPT Days 1123–1129), structure (goals at the start / what came up along the way / where it stands), and its delivered label ("Wavelet 1"). This document is built from the dated record and is consistent with the delivered recap at that level; a line-by-line check against the delivered text is not possible from the durable record, and none is claimed.
- **V15's delivery entry was not located at journal level in this pass.** V15 was green-lit Nov 8 from prepass-3, and the standing record (alignment synthesis) states V15 was delivered before V16 and is not reopened as pending — but no dated "V15 FINAL DELIVERED" entry with hash and gates was found in the Nov 8–9 journals during extraction. The delivery is carried at synthesis strength, flagged here.
- **PR #68 was not individually verified.** MEMORY.md names Claude's phext-lattice PRs #67 and #68 together; only #67's content, merge, deploy, and screen test were verified in the journal spans read. (PR #67: https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/67.)
- **qexo's fleet version state at week's end is layered** — v1.2.0 phextnet live Nov 13, v1.6.1 released and verification-passed Nov 14, the parser repair unmerged — and no single "the fleet runs version X" claim is made for Nov 14.
- **The costs ledger reversed itself inside Nov 14:** the journal first records meters starting at zero with no backfill, then records Will's direction to add back data. The settled state — backfilled — is what this document reports.
- **The token figure is an estimate.** ≈1B is Will's own estimate for the week, stated Nov 15; it is not a metered count, and the ledger's ≈48.5M is an Emise-visible-metering figure only. Both are labeled as what they are wherever they appear.
- **Age label:** parts of the record label the designation day (2026-10-30) as GPT Day 1115; direct date arithmetic from the settled epoch (Day 1 = 2023-10-13) makes it Day 1114. Ages here follow the settled formula (age = GPT Day − 1114), which reproduces all three anchors verified on 2026-11-15. The discrepancy is noted, not silently resolved.

## Certification

> **Retroactively certified by Will Bickford, 2026-11-15.**
>
> Certification was directed by Will in the main chat on 2026-11-15: "Take time to properly document Wavelets 1 and 2 - we retroactively certify them." This document is the Wavelet 2 record under that direction (task 14.4.6/6.6.7/6.5.7). It supersedes, as the formal record of this week, the recap delivered in the main chat on 2026-11-15 under the label "Wavelet 1" — the same week, renumbered by Will's settled count, with the relabeling stated in the open. Certification covers the record as it honestly stands — the measured figures as measured, the estimates labeled as estimates, and the gaps listed above included, not smoothed over.
