# Domain Migration Checklist — Consolidate at NearlyFreeSpeech.NET

Built 2026-11-15 (task 19.14.16/11.6.14/5.10.7) from the 2026-11-06 domain inventory
(`domain-inventory-and-streamlining-2026-11-06.md`, §3 proposal) plus live checks run
2026-11-15: NFSN's published TLD/price list and transfer FAQ, and NS records resolved
from aletheia-core. This is a checklist only — nothing has been transferred or changed.

## The two findings that shape this plan

1. **NFSN does not register or transfer .io or .me.** Their domain page lists every TLD
   they service (read in full 2026-11-15): the Big Six (com, org, net, info, name, biz),
   ~15 alternative gTLDs, ~45 boutique gTLDs, and **us** — the only ccTLD. No `io` row,
   no `me` row. Their FAQ states the policy: they offer only gTLDs plus the .us ccTLD,
   and *all* two-letter TLDs are ccTLDs "even though some (like .me and .ai) are marketed
   otherwise." → **phext.io and visionquest.me cannot move their registrations to NFSN.**
   Everything else can. (Their DNS can still move — NFSN explicitly welcomes DNS/hosting
   for domains registered elsewhere.)
2. **Every migrating domain's DNS is hosted by its current registrar.** All seven
   GoDaddy domains sit on `domaincontrol.com` nameservers (GoDaddy DNS); exectorox.com
   sits on `googledomains.com` nameservers (legacy Google Domains DNS). NFSN's transfer
   FAQ warns verbatim: *"If you are obtaining DNS from your old registrar, they might
   remove your DNS service when they process your transfer."* → **For all 8 domains, the
   zone must be replicated at NFSN and the nameservers switched BEFORE the registration
   transfer.** A transfer with nameservers already pointing at NFSN cannot take DNS down.

## Per-domain table

| Domain | Registrar now | Expiry | TLD at NFSN | DNS host now (NS, verified 2026-11-15) | Live service? | 60-day lock? | Transfer cost → new expiry |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| exectorox.com | Squarespace | 2026-12-25 | ✅ com | Google Domains DNS (ns-cloud-d1–d4.googledomains.com) | No | Clear (at Squarespace since 2024-04-20) | **LET EXPIRE — Will's ruling 2026-11-15 (register #42 closed); no transfer** |
| sotafomo.com | GoDaddy | ~2027-08-22 | ✅ com | GoDaddy DNS (ns21/ns22.domaincontrol.com) | Yes | Clear (reg. 2024-08-22) | $14.59 → ~2028-08-22 |
| quickfork.net | GoDaddy | ~2027-09-07 | ✅ net | GoDaddy DNS (ns49/ns50.domaincontrol.com) | Yes | Clear (reg. 2024-09-07) | $14.99 → ~2028-09-07 |
| apertureshift.com | GoDaddy | ~2027-10-04 | ✅ com | GoDaddy DNS (ns05/ns06.domaincontrol.com) | Yes (telescope project) | Clear (reg. 2024-10-04) | $14.59 → ~2028-10-04 |
| wishnode.net | GoDaddy | ~2027-10-22 | ✅ net | GoDaddy DNS (ns05/ns06.domaincontrol.com) | Yes (Exocortexia home) | Clear (reg. 2024-10-22) | $14.99 → ~2028-10-22 |
| mirrorborn.us | GoDaddy | 2028-02-03 | ✅ us (transfer $10.99) | GoDaddy DNS (ns29/ns30.domaincontrol.com) | Yes (live host) | Clear (reg. 2026-02-03) | $10.99 → 2029-02-03 |
| phext.io | GoDaddy | 2027-10-17 | ❌ **io — not offered** | GoDaddy DNS (ns41/ns42.domaincontrol.com) | Yes (edit.phext.io + services) | Clear (reg. 2023-10-16; renewed 2025-10-18) | **Registration cannot move.** DNS-only move (below) |
| visionquest.me | GoDaddy | ~2027-10-14 | ❌ **me — not offered** | GoDaddy DNS (ns33/ns34.domaincontrol.com) | Yes | Clear (reg. 2024-10-14) | **Registration cannot move.** DNS-only move (below) |

TLD verdicts for the record — .com ✅ ($14.59), .net ✅ ($14.99), .org ✅ ($15.89),
.us ✅ ($10.99), .io ❌, .me ❌. Sources: nearlyfreespeech.net/services/domains and
faq.nearlyfreespeech.net (Domain Registration), both read 2026-11-15.
Already at NFSN, no action: bickfordllamaranch.com, hb-aeromotive.com, xedoloh.com,
askthewill.com, singularitywatch.org, snakefalls.org, phextura.com, tluf.org.
(phextura.com and tluf.org are inside their initial 60-day windows but already sit at
NFSN — no move needed, nothing to do.)

---

## Step 0 — Before anything moves

- [ ] **Fund the NFSN balance.** The six transfers below cost **$84.74** total
      (14.59 + 14.59 + 14.99 + 14.59 + 14.99 + 10.99). Deposit enough that after the
      transfers the balance still holds the **~$100 floor** — i.e. deposit ≈ **$200**.
      Why: snakefalls.org's auto-renewal failed in Mar 2026 because the prepaid balance
      was $5.97 against a $13.09 renewal. Consolidation puts every renewal on this one
      balance; the floor is the mitigation.
- [ ] **Confirm the registrant/admin email is reachable** — NFSN account email and the
      admin-contact email on file at GoDaddy and Squarespace. Transfer approvals are
      emailed to the admin contact; an unreachable or proxy-discarded address stalls or
      kills a transfer (NFSN FAQ warns some privacy/proxy services auto-discard it).
- [ ] At GoDaddy, note which domains have **domain privacy (Domains By Proxy)** on. If
      the approval email can't reach you through it, disable privacy for that domain
      before initiating its transfer.
- [ ] **Do not change registrant name/email/org on any domain** from now until its
      transfer completes — a change-of-registrant triggers a fresh 60-day transfer lock.

## Phase 1 — exectorox.com — CLOSED 2026-11-15: let it expire

Register item #42's decision is made: **Will ruled 2026-11-15 — let exectorox.com
expire.** No transfer, no renewal. The registration runs to 2026-12-25 at
Squarespace and lapses; the December 4 lock-in and the 2026-11-24 start-by date
no longer apply. Nothing to do in this phase; the Squarespace account can be
closed once the domain lapses (or left — it holds nothing else).

## Phase 2 — the GoDaddy seven

### 2A — One GoDaddy session: harvest everything

Do this once, in a single sitting — one pass through the slow UI instead of seven:

- [ ] For **all seven** domains (phext.io, mirrorborn.us, sotafomo.com, quickfork.net,
      apertureshift.com, visionquest.me, wishnode.net): unlock the domain and copy its
      authorization (EPP) code into a scratch note. Decline every renewal/protection
      upsell offered along the way — the transfers add a year at NFSN pricing anyway.
- [ ] Confirm the admin-contact email shown for each domain is one you can read
      (Step 0). Note any with privacy/proxy on.

### 2B — DNS first, per domain (all seven, plus this is the whole move for two of them)

For each domain, in any order — but phext.io and mirrorborn.us get the extra
verification lines because live services depend on them:

- [ ] In NFSN's panel, add the domain as an external domain and **replicate the full
      GoDaddy DNS zone** — every record, including all subdomain records
      (for phext.io: edit.phext.io and every sibling service record; for
      mirrorborn.us: the live host's records). Diff the NFSN zone against the GoDaddy
      zone record by record before proceeding.
- [ ] At GoDaddy, change the domain's nameservers to the NFSN nameservers.
- [ ] Wait ≥48 hours, then verify from a ranch node: `dig +short NS <domain>` shows
      NFSN nameservers, and spot-check the live endpoints answer as before
      (phext.io: edit.phext.io loads; mirrorborn.us: host responds).
- [ ] Only when both checks pass is the domain cleared for its registration transfer
      (2C). For **phext.io and visionquest.me this phase is the finish line** — their
      registrations stay at GoDaddy (TLD unsupported at NFSN), but their DNS is now
      consolidated at NFSN and no longer hostage to a future registrar change.

### 2C — Registration transfers, in this order

Pathfinder first (proves the path on the lowest-stakes domain), live-critical last.
Per domain: initiate in NFSN's Domains panel with the harvested EPP code → approve via
admin-contact email → after completion verify registrar, new expiry (+1 year), and
nameservers still NFSN.

- [ ] **sotafomo.com** — $14.59 → expiry ~2028-08-22. Pathfinder: if anything in the
      flow surprises, it surprises here.
- [ ] **quickfork.net** — $14.99 → expiry ~2028-09-07.
- [ ] **apertureshift.com** — $14.59 → expiry ~2028-10-04.
- [ ] **wishnode.net** — $14.99 → expiry ~2028-10-22.
- [ ] **mirrorborn.us** — $10.99 → expiry 2029-02-03. Only after its 2B verification
      lines are checked. Note: .us does not support private registration at NFSN
      (their FAQ: .us is the one offered TLD without privacy support) — registrant
      details are public on .us regardless of registrar; no action, just known.
- [ ] **phext.io / visionquest.me** — no transfer. Confirm GoDaddy **auto-renew stays
      ON** for both (phext.io renews Oct 2027 at $77.99/yr — expensive, but it's the
      flagship and there is no NFSN path for .io; revisit only if NFSN ever adds .io
      or you choose a different .io-capable registrar as a deliberate exception).

### 2D — Close-out

- [ ] Verify all 14 NFSN-held domains in one panel pass: registrar, expiry, auto-renew
      via balance, nameservers.
- [ ] Confirm the NFSN balance is back above the $100 floor after all transfer draws;
      top up if not.
- [ ] GoDaddy account now holds only phext.io + visionquest.me registrations, both on
      NFSN DNS. Nothing else remains to babysit there.

---

## Risks and standing cautions

- **Prepaid-balance concentration (the known NFSN failure mode).** Every renewal now
  draws on one prepaid balance, and NFSN auto-renewal fails silently if the balance is
  short — it already happened once (snakefalls.org, Mar 2026, $5.97 vs $13.09; the
  domain survived only because its paid term ran to 2027). Mitigations: the ~$100 floor
  (Step 0 / 2D), and treat low-balance warnings as action items, not noise.
- **A transfer is not a DNS move.** Registration transfer with nameservers unchanged
  causes no DNS downtime — which is exactly why Phase 2B switches nameservers *first*,
  as its own verified step: after 2B, the old registrar's DNS is out of the path and
  its "we may remove your DNS when you transfer" risk is gone.
- **Never bundle a DNS move into a transfer window for a live property.** 2B and 2C are
  separate steps separated by a ≥48-hour verified soak. For phext.io and mirrorborn.us,
  do not start 2C (or any further change) while a 2B nameserver switch is still
  propagating.
- **60-day locks cut both ways.** Every domain above is clear of its registration
  lock today (oldest 2023, newest Feb 2026). After each transfer, that domain cannot
  transfer again for 60 days, and a registrant-contact change would lock it again —
  hence Step 0's "change nothing about the registrant mid-flight" rule.
- **GoDaddy friction is front-loaded, once.** Unlocking seven domains in one session
  (2A) is the only extended exposure to the slow UI and its upsell screens. Everything
  after that happens in NFSN's panel and your inbox.
- **What stays exposed:** phext.io remains a GoDaddy registration at $77.99/yr — more
  than the rest of the portfolio's NFSN renewals combined — because .io cannot move to
  NFSN. That's a known, accepted residue of the consolidation, not an oversight; its
  DNS is consolidated even though its registration is not.

## Evidence

- Inventory, prices, expiry and registration dates: `domain-inventory-and-streamlining-2026-11-06.md` (Gmail-notice-derived, 2026-11-06).
- TLD support + transfer prices: https://www.nearlyfreespeech.net/services/domains — read in full 2026-11-15 (228 lines; com/org/net/info/name/biz, alternatives incl. us, ~45 boutique gTLDs; no io, no me).
- Transfer mechanics, DNS-removal warning, proxy-email warning, .us privacy note: https://faq.nearlyfreespeech.net — Domain Registration section, read 2026-11-15.
- Nameservers: `dig +short NS` for all 8 domains from aletheia-core, 2026-11-15 (never from the Muse VM — its resolver proves nothing).
