<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Phextura — Rigorous Delight</title>
<meta name="description" content="Phextura: the phext reformulation of LaTeX. One file. Every idea has an address. Extremely fast to write papers in, extremely readable for humans and machines.">
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" type="image/png">
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
<meta property="og:title" content="Phextura — Rigorous Delight">
<meta property="og:description" content="One file. Every idea has an address.">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:url" content="https://phextura.com/">
<meta property="og:image" content="https://phextura.com/assets/hero.jpg">
<style>
  :root{color-scheme:dark;--bg:#030308;--ink:#f2f0eb;--dim:#b9b4a8;--line:#26262e;--accent:#7dd3fc}
  *{box-sizing:border-box}
  body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.65 Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif}
  a{color:var(--accent)}
  .wrap{max-width:880px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 20px 64px}
  .hero{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin:0 auto}
  .hero-wrap{max-width:720px;margin:0 auto}
  h1{position:absolute;left:-9999px}
  h2{font:600 26px/1.25 system-ui,sans-serif;margin:48px 0 12px;letter-spacing:.01em}
  p{margin:0 0 16px;color:var(--dim)}
  p strong, li strong{color:var(--ink)}
  .lede{font-size:21px;color:var(--ink);text-align:center;margin:28px auto 8px;max-width:640px}
  .tagline{text-align:center;letter-spacing:.35em;text-transform:uppercase;font:600 13px system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--dim);margin:0 0 8px}
  ul{color:var(--dim);padding-left:22px}
  li{margin:0 0 10px}
  .cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:16px;margin:20px 0 8px}
  .card{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:18px;background:#0a0a12}
  .card h3{font:600 17px system-ui,sans-serif;margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--ink)}
  .card p{margin:0;font-size:15.5px}
  code{font:14px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;color:var(--ink);background:#14141e;padding:1px 5px;border-radius:4px}
  .links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin:24px 0}
  .links a{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;padding:9px 18px;text-decoration:none;font:600 15px system-ui,sans-serif;background:#0a0a12}
  .links a:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}
  footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:56px;padding-top:20px;font-size:14.5px;color:var(--dim);display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 24px;justify-content:space-between}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <h1>Phextura — Rigorous Delight</h1>
  <div class="hero-wrap">
    <picture>
      <source srcset="/assets/hero.webp" type="image/webp">
      <img class="hero" src="/assets/hero.jpg" width="1122" height="1402"
           alt="Phextura poster: a plain document flows through a glowing nine-dimensional phext lattice and emerges as a finished paper. One file. Every idea has an address.">
    </picture>
  </div>

  <p class="lede">One file. Every idea has an address.</p>
  <p class="tagline">Rigorous Delight</p>

  <h2>What is Phextura?</h2>
  <p><strong>Phextura is the phext reformulation of LaTeX</strong> — the name succeeds
  LaTeX (Leslie Lamport + Donald Knuth's TeX), rebuilt on a substrate that didn't
  exist in 1978. A LaTeX document is a one-dimensional character stream that a
  macro expander executes. A Phextura document is a <strong>phext corpus</strong>:
  plain-text scrolls at deterministic addresses in a nine-dimensional lattice
  (<code>Library.Shelf.Series / Collection.Volume.Book / Chapter.Section.Scroll</code>).
  Structure is not simulated on top of the stream. Structure <em>is</em> the addressing.</p>

  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Fast to write</h3>
      <p>No preamble ritual, no escaping regime, no rerun-until-the-labels-settle.
      Write prose in scrolls, address the parts, cite by address.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Readable by humans and machines</h3>
      <p>A scroll is plain text a person can read raw — and trivially machine-readable,
      because its identity and role are its coordinate, not the side effects of executing it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Everything inside the file</h3>
      <p>Graphics, media, and embedded documents of any type ride in the corpus itself.
      A paper can even hoist its own toolchain — a compiler, a copy of libphext,
      a proof checker — and carry its proofs as addressed scrolls.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Global addresses</h2>
  <p>Phextura establishes the <strong>first global address scheme for phext</strong>:
  addresses that are durable <em>between</em> Phextura files — distinct from phext
  addresses, which are internal to each phext. Durable global addresses are what
  let multiple Phextura files compose easily: cite a theorem in another paper the
  same way you cite one in your own, and the reference is the link.</p>

  <h2>Rigorous Delight</h2>
  <p>Every element must be both: <strong>rigorous</strong> — derivable, checkable,
  costed — and <strong>delightful</strong>. Rigor alone is homework. Delight alone
  is a toy.</p>

  <div class="links">
    <a href="https://github.com/wbic16/phextura">GitHub — wbic16/phextura</a>
    <a href="https://phext.io/">phext.io</a>
    <a href="https://edit.phext.io/">Phext Edit</a>
  </div>

  <footer>
    <span>Phextura — a project by Will Bickford</span>
    <span>phextura.com · 2026</span>
  </footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
